    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-07T18:03:53+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-07T18:03:53+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T07:33:53Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T07:33:53Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred well south of SA will continue to drift eastwards over the weekend, while a developing low pressure system and trough in WA move close to the SA border. The high drifts southeast of Tasmania by Monday as the low moves across western SA on Monday and northern SA on Tuesday before clearing to the east later. Another high develops south of the bight on Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW004" description="Upper South East" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-07T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly clear. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h becoming light in the late evening.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. The chance of frost south of Keith in the early morning. Light winds becoming easterly 15 to 20 km/h in the morning then becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 4 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 4:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the morning then becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 7 with daytime temperatures reaching the high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny morning. The chance of a thunderstorm with little or no rainfall near the eastern border in the afternoon. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h shifting south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 13 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower near the coast, near zero chance elsewhere. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
